<Layout title="Infrastructure" description="Research infrastructure and data sources of the Heliophysics and Space Weather group at USACH: HPC cluster, pilot space weather platform, and magnetometry.">

<section>
  <span class="section-title">Infrastructure</span>
  <h1>Infrastructure and data</h1>
  <p class="lead">The computing, instrumentation, and data behind our heliophysics and space weather research.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="card stack-card">
    <h3>High-performance computing (HPC) cluster</h3>
    <p>Computing platform at the Department of Physics, funded by FONDEQUIP (2023) and directed by Dr. Victor Pinto. Used to train machine learning models, process large satellite datasets, and run numerical simulations.</p>
    <p class="meta"><a href="https://fisica.usach.cl/es/plataforma-de-investigacion-hpc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HPC platform, USACH Department of Physics</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack-card">
    <h3>Pilot space weather platform (FONDEF IDEA)</h3>
    <p>Project led by Universidad Adventista de Chile (UnACh), with USACH as partner institution (2025-2027). It develops a pilot system for real-time space weather monitoring and early warnings in Chile, with deep-learning forecasting models.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack-card">
    <h3>Magnetometry</h3>
    <p>Performance evaluation of magnetometers for geomagnetic monitoring, in collaboration with UnACh (<a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/s26154700" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Caro et al., 2026, <em>Sensors</em></a>), and analysis of ground magnetometer network data to study geomagnetic disturbances and geomagnetically induced currents (GIC).</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="section-title">Data we use</span>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Satellites</h3>
      <p>Van Allen Probes (MagEIS, REPT, EMFISIS, EFW) · THEMIS (SPEDAS) · GOES · OMNI</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ground networks</h3>
      <p>Magnetometers: SAMBA · MACCS · THEMIS GBO · CARISMA. SuperDARN radars</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Tools</h3>
      <p>Python (NumPy, SciPy, pandas, Matplotlib, SpacePy) · TensorFlow/Keras · PyTorch · scikit-learn</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
